<article class="env-lemma" id="0GGC">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GGC">Lemma <span data-tag="0GGC">88.14.5</span>.</a> Let $\varphi : A \to B$ be an arrow of $\textit{WAdm}^{Noeth}$ which is adic and topologically of finite type. Let $\mathfrak q \subset B$ be rig-closed. If $A/I$ is Jacobson for some ideal of definition $I \subset A$, then $\mathfrak p = \varphi ^{-1}(\mathfrak q) \subset A$ is rig-closed. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/0GGA" data-tag="0GGA">88.14.3</a> (combined with Lemma <a href="/tag/0GC5" data-tag="0GC5">88.12.4</a>) the residue field $\kappa $ of $B/\mathfrak q$ is of finite type over $A/\mathfrak a$. Since $A/\mathfrak a$ is Jacobson, we see that $\kappa $ is finite over $A/\mathfrak a$ by Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0CY7" data-tag="0CY7">10.35.18</a>. We conclude by Lemma <a href="/tag/0GGB" data-tag="0GGB">88.14.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>